{
	chapter.0C8D53A7E1264BF9.title: "Era 3 - Petrochemical Civilization"
	chapter.0C8D53A7E1264BF9.subtitle: "Refine the dead world's buried chemistry into fuel, polymers, and control"
	chapter.2034B9BBF53C750D.title: "Feeding the Domain"
	chapter.2034B9BBF53C750D.subtitle: "From gathered crops to civilization-scale food logistics"
	chapter.6B00D00000000001.title: "Brewery and Winery"
	chapter.6B00D00000000001.subtitle: "From field crops and pressed fruit to fermentation and cellar maturation"
	quest.6B01000000000001.title: "Three Fermentation Crops"
	quest.6B01000000000001.quest_desc: ["Brewery turns grapes, barley, and hops into a complete Create-powered fermentation chain. Establish renewable stock of all three crops; this optional line begins after the Mechanical Foundation and never gates an era."]
	quest.6B01000000000002.title: "Malt and Bittering"
	quest.6B01000000000002.quest_desc: ["Smoke prepared barley into kilned malt and boil hops in a heated basin. These are process intermediates, not arbitrary collection targets: malt supplies fermentable grain while hops give beer its bittering stage."]
	quest.6B01000000000003.title: "Mash and Living Culture"
	quest.6B01000000000003.quest_desc: ["Press apples and Brewery grapes into mash, then culture Brewer's Yeast from sugar and water. The yeast is a manufactured fermentation input; preserve enough crop stock to repeat the process rather than consuming the last harvest."]
	quest.6B01000000000004.title: "Brewery's Three Vats"
	quest.6B01000000000004.quest_desc: ["Use heated Create mixing to produce representative Brewery batches: beer from malt, boiled hops, yeast, and water; cider from apple mash; and wine from grape mash. One bucket of each proves the fluid process without demanding every decorative mug variant."]
	quest.6B01000000000005.title: "Create Winery's Two Grapes"
	quest.6B01000000000005.quest_desc: ["Create Winery adds separate red and white grape bushes for cellar production. Establish renewable examples of both. Their ordinary habitat is plains and forest-type biomes, so preserve bushes or propagation stock before committing fruit to processing."]
	quest.6B01000000000006.title: "Press for Pomace and Must"
	quest.6B01000000000006.quest_desc: ["Create compacting presses three matching grapes into red or white pomace; apples become Apple Must. These solids are the Wine Cellar's maturation feedstocks and distinguish Winery's bottled products from Brewery's bulk fermented fluids."]
	quest.6B01000000000007.title: "Build the Wine Cellar"
	quest.6B01000000000007.quest_desc: ["Create Winery's Wine Cellar matures pomace or must into finished bottles. Build one with established Create materials, keep its input recipes visible in JEI, and treat maturation time as production capacity rather than a reason to build an unmaintainable wall of cellars."]
	quest.6B01000000000008.title: "A Representative Cellar Reserve"
	quest.6B01000000000008.quest_desc: ["Mature one representative red wine, white wine, and cider at small settlement scale. Bordeaux, Chardonnay, and Cider prove all three feedstock families without turning the quest book into a catalogue of every flavor variant. The products are detected, not consumed."]
	chapter.1240CAEABAC9DC56.title: "The Workday Beverage Economy"
	chapter.1240CAEABAC9DC56.subtitle: "Coffee and tea do not feed you; they help you get the work done"
	chapter_group.3F00D00000000001.title: "Industrial Food Production"
	quest.08F11D0000000001.title: "A Long Day Ahead"
	quest.08F11D0000000001.quest_desc: ["No compatible Create Cafe build is installed, so acclimatized crops feed Infinite Domain's native Create processing line." "Cultivate eight coffee cherries."]
	quest.08F11D0000000002.title: "Not Food, Still Breakfast"
	quest.08F11D0000000002.quest_desc: ["Coffee restores no hunger or saturation. Its value is affordable Haste and Speed for ordinary work." "Brew one black coffee."]
	quest.08F11D0000000003.title: "The Daily Grind"
	quest.08F11D0000000003.quest_desc: ["Wash, roast, and mechanically mill beans into standardized brewing feed." "Produce sixteen coffee grounds."]
	quest.08F11D0000000004.title: "Put the Kettle On"
	quest.08F11D0000000004.quest_desc: ["Green tea lasts longer and favors travel; black tea trades some duration for Haste." "Brew one green tea."]
	quest.08F11D0000000005.title: "Another Cup"
	quest.08F11D0000000005.quest_desc: ["Espresso provides a short Haste II burst, but remains weaker overall than advanced energy drinks." "Prepare one espresso."]
	quest.08F11D0000000006.title: "Take It With You"
	quest.08F11D0000000006.quest_desc: ["Shared cans turn café fluids into portable industrial consumer goods." "Can twelve coffees."]
	quest.08F11D0000000007.title: "Break Room Supplies"
	quest.08F11D0000000007.quest_desc: ["Six-packs and cases conserve every drink while simplifying distribution." "Package one coffee case."]
	quest.08F11D0000000008.title: "The Night Shift"
	quest.08F11D0000000008.quest_desc: ["A tea crate proves the branching leaf-processing line can sustain shipment-scale output." "Create one tea crate."]
	quest.08F11D0000000009.title: "Industrial Beverage Service"
	quest.08F11D0000000009.quest_desc: ["Four crates become one freight pallet with every can conserved exactly." "Palletize one coffee shipment."]
	quest.7B2B0CE2A9CEAD24.title: "Dry the Harvest"
	quest.7B2B0CE2A9CEAD24.quest_desc: ["Smoking makes herbs shelf-stable and ready for factory handling." "Produce eight dried culinary herbs."]
	quest.7CF96E34F433B244.title: "Mill Standard Spices"
	quest.7CF96E34F433B244.quest_desc: ["Milling turns varied crops into a predictable aromatic ingredient." "Produce eight ground spice."]
	quest.60C6255859EF43EB.title: "Standardize Seasoning"
	quest.60C6255859EF43EB.quest_desc: ["Salt, herbs, and spice become one reusable industrial recipe input." "Mix eight prepared seasoning packets."]
	quest.62B68B083A9340FD.title: "Crush the First Fruit"
	quest.62B68B083A9340FD.quest_desc: ["Fruit processing now rewards machinery with pulp and useful pomace." "Make four apple pulp."]
	quest.0025674D5053D8CD.title: "Concentrate the Harvest"
	quest.0025674D5053D8CD.quest_desc: ["Concentrate moves fruit value through the factory without hauling raw crops." "Produce four apple juice concentrate."]
	quest.5B113F3538B71374.title: "Bottle a Manufactured Drink"
	quest.5B113F3538B71374.quest_desc: ["Manufactured food has better staying power than crude meals. Juices also differ slightly: apple is filling, berry aids recovery, and orange supports short work bursts." "Bottle four apple juices, then experiment with the other flavors."]
	quest.3CE261E9EC4CF123.title: "Reduce the Broth"
	quest.3CE261E9EC4CF123.quest_desc: ["A heated vegetable fluid line supplies kitchens without repeating hand recipes." "Prepare four concentrated soup bases."]
	quest.1BD60D82F5AB7FB3.title: "Capture Fermentation Gas"
	quest.1BD60D82F5AB7FB3.quest_desc: ["A reusable culture converts sugar feed into process carbon dioxide for later carbonation." "Prepare one food-grade culture."]
	quest.36DCF312DDFCF7DD.title: "Feed a Settlement"
	quest.36DCF312DDFCF7DD.quest_desc: ["Protein, vegetables, starch, seasoning, and oil outperform monoculture cooking." "Produce eight prepared settlement meals."]
	quest.6220EA917425C59A.title: "Stamp Beverage Cans"
	quest.6220EA917425C59A.quest_desc: ["Aluminum plate connects metallurgy directly to drink production." "Stamp sixteen empty beverage cans."]
	quest.5CAA77912D413E80.title: "Form Heavy Food Cans"
	quest.5CAA77912D413E80.quest_desc: ["Steel packaging enables durable preserved meals." "Form eight empty food cans."]
	quest.066534B9EED187AC.title: "Seal Industrial Stew"
	quest.066534B9EED187AC.quest_desc: ["Hot filling and sealing turn prepared meals into expedition-ready stores." "Produce eight canned stews."]
	quest.271FC2FC3F6540D6.title: "Carbonate a Flavor Line"
	quest.271FC2FC3F6540D6.quest_desc: ["Blend concentrate and syrup, inject captured carbon dioxide, then fill cans." "Produce six apple soda cans."]
	quest.17E87207E385EF52.title: "Bundle Consumer Goods"
	quest.17E87207E385EF52.quest_desc: ["Small reversible packages trade a little space for convenient logistics." "Assemble two berry soda six-packs."]
	quest.52233AEAB76458BB.title: "Case the Product"
	quest.52233AEAB76458BB.quest_desc: ["Cases are the first true shipment-scale beverage unit." "Package one orange soda case."]
	quest.077D16DFAD15DC23.title: "Prepare Food-Grade Electrolytes"
	quest.077D16DFAD15DC23.quest_desc: ["Refined mineral inputs support advanced drinks without using absurdly hazardous chemistry." "Produce eight electrolyte blends."]
	quest.2C3D3B6833E06D5A.title: "Extract a Stimulant"
	quest.2C3D3B6833E06D5A.quest_desc: ["Agriculture and chemistry meet in a controlled stimulant ingredient." "Refine four stimulant extracts."]
	quest.52F44BCFA17D8586.title: "Manufacture Energy Drinks"
	quest.52F44BCFA17D8586.quest_desc: ["Concentrate, syrup, purified water, electrolytes, stimulant, and carbonation complete the advanced line." "Can twelve energy drinks."]
	quest.04D44ABE4F6F2CB8.title: "Crate Mixed Beverages"
	quest.04D44ABE4F6F2CB8.quest_desc: ["Different drinks are useful rather than interchangeable: apple favors saturation, berry favors recovery, orange favors movement, and energy drinks favor factory work." "Assemble one mixed beverage crate."]
	quest.67DA49934330E1EF.title: "Assemble Field Rations"
	quest.67DA49934330E1EF.quest_desc: ["Entrée, crackers, fruit, beverage powder, and condiment become a portable near-complete meal with exceptional staying power." "Produce eight complete field rations."]
	quest.4F9A7C40B90A12EA.title: "Case Expedition Supplies"
	quest.4F9A7C40B90A12EA.quest_desc: ["Ration cases make individual meals practical for settlement logistics." "Package two ration cases."]
	quest.6D81BAB21AF3A8A5.title: "Palletize Expedition Supplies"
	quest.6D81BAB21AF3A8A5.quest_desc: ["Four military ration crates lock onto one freight pallet without changing the number of meals inside." "Deliver one ration pallet."]
	quest.50503724FC646207.title: "Stock Advanced Beverages"
	quest.50503724FC646207.quest_desc: ["Energy drinks trade some nutrition for short Speed and Haste. They support a work shift without replacing potions or meals." "Package four energy-drink cases."]
	quest.6058218448311BFE.title: "Feed the Infinite Domain"
	quest.6058218448311BFE.quest_desc: ["The final milestone is repeatable freight: each pallet preserves exactly four mixed crates and every can they contain." "Deliver two mixed beverage pallets."]
	chapter.0FD581D87A58E08D.title: "Era 6 - High Energy and Nuclear Engineering"
	chapter.0FD581D87A58E08D.subtitle: "High-output systems operating under permanent radiological accountability"
	chapter.1060266057D3D466.title: "Era 0 - Lost Survivors"
	chapter.1060266057D3D466.subtitle: "Shelter, water, food, salvage, and the first defensible settlement"
	chapter.1B7E40C69A25D8F3.title: "Sustenance, Medicine and Habitation"
	chapter.1B7E40C69A25D8F3.subtitle: "Keep a settlement alive long enough for industry to matter"
	chapter.2127F3E4D2A0546E.title: "Prologue - Another Lost Soul"
	chapter.2127F3E4D2A0546E.subtitle: "Connection established // identity, interface, and immediate survival"
	chapter.2EE181FAE3A636DA.title: "Era 4 - The Electrical Grid"
	chapter.2EE181FAE3A636DA.subtitle: "Generation, distribution, protection, and public electrical service"
	chapter.37550227CA365A64.title: "Era 2 - Heavy Industry"
	chapter.37550227CA365A64.subtitle: "Steel, furnaces, rail, and extraction beyond hand labor"
	chapter.37AF8051C9D264BE.title: "Era 5 - Automated Industry"
	chapter.37AF8051C9D264BE.subtitle: "Machines that remember, route, fabricate, and maintain production"
	chapter.381AB56C38F92B73.title: "Cyberware Ascension"
	chapter.381AB56C38F92B73.subtitle: "Clinical augmentation, donor salvage, and the cost of replacing flesh"
	chapter.3A128F94DD7C5061.title: "Era 8 - Infinite Domain"
	chapter.3A128F94DD7C5061.subtitle: "Civilization-scale systems with no surviving external authority"
	chapter.5A1C0E7D93B246F8.title: "Era 1 - Mechanical Reconstruction"
	chapter.5A1C0E7D93B246F8.subtitle: "Turn isolated labor into repeatable mechanical production"
	chapter.68E1A7C4D9302B5F.title: "Applied Energistics Recovery"
	chapter.68E1A7C4D9302B5F.subtitle: "Recover storage, channels, autocrafting, and damaged network technology"
	chapter.6CFF000000000001.title: "Spawn Exchange"
	chapter.6CFF000000000001.subtitle: "Authorized settlement vendors, stock manifests, and physical coin prices"
	chapter.74C2D8A15E903BF6.title: "Air, Sea and Global Logistics"
	chapter.74C2D8A15E903BF6.subtitle: "Move people and cargo farther than local roads can support"
	chapter.79D40B1DF769CB1A.title: "Era 7 - Orbital Industry"
	chapter.79D40B1DF769CB1A.subtitle: "Life support, launch systems, extraterrestrial material, and permanent flight"
	chapter.051D98EED36CF87B.title: "Early Livestock Exchange"
	chapter.051D98EED36CF87B.subtitle: "Rebuild viable herds without depending on random animal migration"
	chapter.7000000000000000.title: "Era 0 Mastery — Lost Survivors"
	chapter.7000000000000000.subtitle: "Optional civilization-scale proof that survival resources are no longer scarce"
	chapter_group.346E9B7B176D7846.title: "Civilization Eras"
	chapter_group.7C5A000000000001.title: "Space Industrialization"
	chapter_group.4D9B7E21A6C850F3.title: "Global Logistics"
	chapter_group.6F2A9C4D8E1B7305.title: "Survivor Exchange"
	chapter_group.7ADA55C0FFEE0001.title: "Civilization Mastery"
	quest.03D683A19D0589EE.quest_desc: [
		"Run Scrap Piles through your String Mesh. Garbage bags are the first useful junk intermediate: they can be processed again rather than magically becoming clean metal."
		"The odds are harsh. Accumulate inputs, work together, and treat every recovered component as evidence that the process functions."
	]
	quest.03D683A19D0589EE.title: "Junk Becomes Feedstock"
	quest.0764B2D3F8A1CE95.quest_desc: [
		"Eggs, feathers, and compact renewable food make chickens unusually valuable."
		"This exchange supplies one spawn egg and can be repeated."
	]
	quest.0764B2D3F8A1CE95.title: "Chicken Spawn Egg - 2 Sprockets"
	quest.08C9F0A01B505526.quest_desc: [
		"An Item Vault is a high-throughput bulk buffer. Extend it in one axis, connect insertion and extraction at deliberate points, and remember that large capacity does not correct a deadlocked line."
		"A Depot holds one processing stack where presses, deployers, and funnels can reach it. Use Depots for controlled work positions and Vaults for flow buffering; they are different objects because they solve different problems."
		"Obtain one Item Vault and four Depots. The task detects them without consuming them; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.08C9F0A01B505526.title: "Buffer the Production Line"
	quest.0D2120E425BA76F6.quest_desc: [
		"Vanilla wooden, stone, gold, iron, and diamond tools have only one point of durability here. They remain as recipe components and artifacts, not dependable equipment."
		"Craft Primitive Start bone tools. Begin with a pickaxe, axe, and shovel; these are crude, but crude is worlds better than helpless."
	]
	quest.0D2120E425BA76F6.title: "An Arsenal of Remains"
	quest.0FFBED0140C896F0.quest_desc: [
		"Dead bushes and ferns are more valuable than they appear. They provide sticks and seeds, and Infinite Domain gives each a very small chance to reveal scrap metal."
		"Ferns also have a small chance to drop themselves. Unlike sticks, plant matter can become compost. Preserve anything that still grows."
		"This opens the Farming route. Follow its heart-shaped quests to turn water, ruined soil, and biological scraps into renewable habitation."
	]
	quest.0FFBED0140C896F0.title: "Life in the Dust"
	quest.13B2E88DD6707ABA.quest_desc: [
		"A Stack Upgrade multiplies how much each slot can hold. Install the first tier in a compatible storage block and confirm the new slot limits before routing automated production into it."
		"Capacity upgrades improve density, not organization. A larger container filled with unrelated debris is merely a more ambitious debris problem."
		"Obtain one Tier 1 Stack Upgrade. The task detects it without consuming it; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.13B2E88DD6707ABA.title: "Denser Stores"
	quest.14C99AF95E39DE33.quest_desc: [
		"Connect two parallel shafts with a Mechanical Belt, then place an item on its upper surface. Rotation determines travel direction; reverse the network if the belt confidently delivers everything to the wrong end."
		"Depots provide stationary work positions beside a belt. Funnels insert or extract. Build a short test line before routing the settlement's entire inventory through your first attempt."
		"Obtain eight Belt Connectors. The task detects them without consuming them; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.14C99AF95E39DE33.title: "The First Conveyor"
	quest.1C55B64184822DE7.quest_desc: [
		"Construct an Ex Deorum sieve. Its frame is intentionally expensive: even the first sieve represents lumber, prepared components, and a stable working site."
		"Place the String Mesh into the sieve, then process gravel, sand, dust, Scrap Piles, radioactive waste, and ruined barrels. Consult JEI for the exact mesh-dependent results."
	]
	quest.1C55B64184822DE7.title: "The First Sieve"
	quest.1CE40D15564FEADC.quest_desc: ["Review the three Era 0 professions: Scavenging recovers the ruins, Masonry creates the furnace-scale stone reserve, and Habitation rebuilds water, soil, food, and medicine. Any one completed charter can reach the furnace capstone."]
	quest.1CE40D15564FEADC.title: "Choose How You Will Survive"
	quest.217F49A41737D832.quest_desc: ["Combine compressed coarse dirt, compressed clay, and water through the reclamation recipe to obtain a grass block."]
	quest.217F49A41737D832.title: "A Patch of Green"
	quest.227CBFC089E818C2.quest_desc: [
		"A cheap source of wool, mutton, and eventually beds."
		"This exchange supplies one spawn egg and can be repeated."
	]
	quest.227CBFC089E818C2.title: "Sheep Spawn Egg - 1 Bevel"
	quest.239E78568F697EDA.quest_desc: [
		"Funnels move items horizontally between belts and inventories. Their arrow indicates direction; use a wrench to reverse one instead of rebuilding the factory around a misplaced funnel."
		"Chutes move items vertically and can connect stacked processing floors. Filters keep shared lines from becoming a democratic mixture of every material you own."
		"Obtain four Andesite Funnels and four Chutes. The task detects them without consuming them; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.239E78568F697EDA.title: "Route Items Deliberately"
	quest.28D17AA502A74353.quest_desc: [
		"Install a Pickup Upgrade to pull nearby dropped items into the container. Configure its filter unless your design goal is to collect every loose object within reach, including the ones you were still using."
		"A Hopper Upgrade moves items through a chosen face. Open its settings, select input or output, and verify the side against the block preview before blaming the destination inventory."
		"Obtain one Pickup Upgrade and one Hopper Upgrade. The task detects them without consuming them; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.28D17AA502A74353.title: "Collect the Output"
	quest.29B0744D12BCCA8C.quest_desc: [
		"A dependable source of pork once a breeding pair is established."
		"This exchange supplies one spawn egg and can be repeated."
	]
	quest.29B0744D12BCCA8C.title: "Pig Spawn Egg - 2 Bevels"
	quest.2C1F9877A3002405.quest_desc: ["Obtain 8 canned food, 4 purified water, and 4 bandages. These are survival reserves, not permission to neglect renewable food and clean-water systems."]
	quest.2C1F9877A3002405.title: "Emergency Stores"
	quest.2EC908A6609C17D6.quest_desc: ["Combine nine 1× compressed cobblestone into one 2× block: 81 ordinary cobblestone per block."]
	quest.2EC908A6609C17D6.title: "Stone Under Pressure"
	quest.3708666FE05834A4.quest_desc: ["Secure a water bucket. In the wasteland, water is both survival stock and a crafting reagent; container-return recipes give the empty bucket back where specified."]
	quest.3708666FE05834A4.title: "Water Is Civilization"
	quest.37553E8B6284E8E2.quest_desc: [
		"Fire contained. Heat repeated. Material transformed on demand. This humble furnace is the first machine your new civilization can claim as its own."
		"You are not out of the Stone Age yet—but for the first time, leaving it is no longer theoretical."
		"Completing any one professional contribution opens Era 1. The other two routes remain available, because allies and settlements profit from completing all three."
	]
	quest.37553E8B6284E8E2.title: "A Fire That Belongs to Us"
	quest.3A30BF9375157C30.quest_desc: [
		"Prepare Beef Stew in the Cooking Pot and supply bowls for extraction. The pot accepts ingredients from above and can place completed servings into an adjacent container when arranged correctly."
		"Automate only after confirming every crop and animal input is renewable. Consuming the breeding stock to demonstrate food automation would be memorable, but not in the way I intend."
		"Obtain four servings of Beef Stew. The task detects them without consuming them; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.3A30BF9375157C30.title: "Feed the Whole Shift"
	quest.3A97E5062BD4F1C8.quest_desc: [
		"Rabbit hide, meat, and feet are specialized supplies rather than staples."
		"This exchange supplies one spawn egg and can be repeated."
	]
	quest.3A97E5062BD4F1C8.title: "Rabbit Spawn Egg - 3 Sprockets"
	quest.3AFBE38263D3351E.quest_desc: [
		"Ambition can wait. The night will not. Claim a room, a cave, a cellar, or a hole in the earth. Block entrances, establish a retreat, and remember where it is."
		"The central continent is a wasteland. Coarse dirt is common; ordinary dirt, living plants, clean water, and intact materials are resources rather than scenery."
		"From here the chapter divides into three readable routes: hexagons for Mining, hearts for Farming, and diamonds for Exploration. Gears mark technical support or optional side work; octagons mark major convergence points. Any one profession route can complete an era, while side branches remain useful without becoming hidden gates."
	]
	quest.3AFBE38263D3351E.title: "Shelter Before Ambition"
	quest.3C516B726E0141E2.quest_desc: ["Produce nine normal dirt through the pack’s reclamation chain. Wasteland coarse dirt is not interchangeable with ordinary dirt."]
	quest.3C516B726E0141E2.title: "Make Living Dirt"
	quest.3E6BEAE3F78C8F4B.quest_desc: [
		"A sieve frame does nothing without mesh. String mesh is the poorest available grade, which makes it perfect for us."
		"Mesh grades determine which results are possible. Better mesh does not simply mean more of the same—it opens different salvage categories."
		"Ex Deorum guarantees a fallback result for every Infinite Domain salvage input, but richer outcomes still depend on material and mesh tier. Check JEI before spending a rare input."
	]
	quest.3E6BEAE3F78C8F4B.title: "A Net for Dust"
	quest.463D483C4FED56D3.quest_desc: [
		"Compression is the central accounting system of Infinite Domain. Nine ordinary blocks become one 1x compressed block; nine 1x blocks become one 2x block."
		"Compressed ingredients appear throughout the pack wherever a machine or structure should represent community-scale investment. Begin with cobblestone."
		"AllTheCompressed is not optional storage convenience here: its blocks are the pack's language for labor, logistics, and settlement-scale cost."
	]
	quest.463D483C4FED56D3.title: "Introduction to Compression"
	quest.48BC4708142777F2.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade the capacity multiplier only where throughput justifies it. Reserve dense storage for stable bulk materials and keep working buffers small enough that failures remain visible."
		"Replacing every Tier 1 upgrade immediately is not planning. It is enthusiasm wearing an inventory-management costume."
		"Obtain one Tier 2 Stack Upgrade. The task detects it without consuming it; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.48BC4708142777F2.title: "Storage Specialist"
	quest.48C4834A084A697D.quest_desc: [
		"Sophisticated Storage provides upgradeable chests and barrels for compact workshop buffering."
		"Place a Sophisticated Chest or Barrel where you can still reach its front face. Open it and inspect the upgrade slots before spending components; yes, checking whether a device accepts an upgrade is traditionally done before manufacturing the upgrade."
		"Chests expose their contents conventionally. Barrels are excellent compact buffers and can display stored material. Keep either accessible until you understand its controls."
		"Obtain one Sophisticated Chest and one Sophisticated Barrel. The task detects them without consuming them; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.48C4834A084A697D.title: "Storage Worth Upgrading"
	quest.4B2A9ADF7B47B7EF.quest_desc: ["The dead still wander beyond protected ground. Kill one zombie when you are armed and ready; this optional lesson confirms that ordinary night travel is not safe merely because dawn exists."]
	quest.4B2A9ADF7B47B7EF.title: "The Dead Still Walk"
	quest.4CAC8CDFA63C7410.quest_desc: [
		"Ex Deorum begins with force rather than finesse. A wooden hammer breaks basic materials into forms that can be sifted and recombined."
		"The pack's Ex Deorum settings are deliberately slow and sparse. One survivor can begin the process; a settlement can make it practical."
		"Use JEI's recipe categories to distinguish hammering from sieving. They are connected processes, not interchangeable recipes."
	]
	quest.4CAC8CDFA63C7410.title: "Reduction by Impact"
	quest.4CCA9DDD52BF8576.quest_desc: [
		"The Skillet cooks held ingredients directly and prepares several meals without constructing the full pot assembly. Inspect each recipe in JEI; ingredients do not become compatible merely because they fit in your hand."
		"Use it for flexible field cooking, then move repeated settlement recipes into the maintained kitchen."
		"Obtain one Skillet. The task detects it without consuming it; this support lesson does not gate the era."
	]
	quest.4CCA9DDD52BF8576.title: "Meals Beyond the Campfire"
	quest.4D3BDA6807AB73A9.quest_desc: [
		"The dead carry the first workable material in abundance: bone. Zombies can drop bones in Infinite Domain, though acquiring them is neither dignified nor safe."
		"Primitive Start turns bone and sticks into tools capable of beginning the work that ruined vanilla tools cannot sustain."
		"This opens the Mining route. Follow its hexagonal quests from bone tools through hammering, quarrying, and compression. Primitive Start bone recipes are deliberately exempt from expensive stick substitutions."
	]
	quest.4D3BDA6807AB73A9.title: "The Dead Provide"
	quest.4FBD65644FB8B833.quest_desc: ["Mine 64 cobblestone with the primitive tools restored by this pack. This is the first measured stone reserve on the Mason route."]
	quest.4FBD65644FB8B833.title: "A Stack of Stone"
	quest.5A00000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Applied Energistics 2 (AE2) turns recovered certus into a shared digital storage and automation network."
		"Recover enough certus quartz to prove that the strange crystal is a repeatable material rather than a curiosity."
		"Objective: obtain 16 × Certus Quartz Crystal. The terminal detects these items without consuming them."
	]
	quest.5A00000000000001.title: "Certus Is Evidence"
	quest.5A00000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"Enter an AE2 meteorite. FTB Quests detects the registered structure itself; standing beside a crater is not enough."
		"Objective: enter Meteorite. The terminal verifies the generated structure while you stand inside it."
	]
	quest.5A00000000000002.title: "The Fallen Archive"
	quest.5A00000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"Recover the engineering press and preserve it as shared infrastructure."
		"Objective: obtain 1 × Engineering Processor Press. The terminal detects these items without consuming them."
	]
	quest.5A00000000000003.title: "Presses From the Sky"
	quest.5A00000000000004.quest_desc: [
		"Rebuild the Inscriber and establish a protected processor workshop."
		"Objective: obtain 1 × Inscriber. The terminal detects these items without consuming them."
	]
	quest.5A00000000000004.title: "Inscribed Logic"
	quest.5A00000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"Commission the first intentionally limited ME storage appliance."
