	quest.6101100000000001.title: "Jaffa Quest: Establish the Orange Grove"
	quest.6101100000000001.quest_desc: ["Recover an orange sapling from Jaffabricate world generation and establish a renewable grove. The production line must not depend on stripping the last wild tree." "This optional miniature line belongs to late Era 1 Create automation and does not block the Mechanical Foundation capstone. Item tasks detect inventory contents without consuming them." ]
	quest.6101100000000002.title: "Jaffa Quest: Juice and Jelly"
	quest.6101100000000002.quest_desc: ["Compact oranges into juice, then mix 250 mB of juice with slime for each jelly. Bottling one sample proves the spout and fluid route are working." "This optional miniature line belongs to late Era 1 Create automation and does not block the Mechanical Foundation capstone. Item tasks detect inventory contents without consuming them." ]
	quest.6101100000000003.title: "Jaffa Quest: Sponge, Jelly, Chocolate"
	quest.6101100000000003.quest_desc: ["Heat flour, sugar, and egg into a base, deploy the orange jelly, then apply 250 mB of Create chocolate. This is the complete individual Jaffa production cycle." "This optional miniature line belongs to late Era 1 Create automation and does not block the Mechanical Foundation capstone. Item tasks detect inventory contents without consuming them." ]
	quest.6101100000000004.title: "Jaffa Quest: Print the Boxes"
	quest.6101100000000004.quest_desc: ["Press pulp into Create cardboard, deploy both package dyes during sequenced assembly, and compact the resulting paperboard into an empty branded box." "This optional miniature line belongs to late Era 1 Create automation and does not block the Mechanical Foundation capstone. Item tasks detect inventory contents without consuming them." ]
	quest.6101100000000005.title: "Jaffa Quest: Ten to a Box"
	quest.6101100000000005.quest_desc: ["Run the box through ten sequenced-assembly loops. Each completed box represents exactly ten finished Jaffa cakes; a single lucky cake is no longer enough." "This optional miniature line belongs to late Era 1 Create automation and does not block the Mechanical Foundation capstone. Item tasks detect inventory contents without consuming them." ]
	quest.6101100000000006.title: "Jaffa Quest: Twenty-Four Boxes to a Pallet"
	quest.6101100000000006.quest_desc: ["Cut or craft an empty pallet and deploy twenty-four completed boxes through its assembly loop. One full pallet therefore represents 240 Jaffa cakes." "This optional miniature line belongs to late Era 1 Create automation and does not block the Mechanical Foundation capstone. Item tasks detect inventory contents without consuming them." ]
	quest.6101100000000007.title: "Jaffa Quest: Band the Load"
	quest.6101100000000007.quest_desc: ["Deploy string onto the full pallet to produce the finished transport-safe Jaffa pallet. The packaging is part of the factory, not decorative waste." "This optional miniature line belongs to late Era 1 Create automation and does not block the Mechanical Foundation capstone. Item tasks detect inventory contents without consuming them." ]
	quest.6101100000000008.title: "Jaffa Export Contract"
	quest.6101100000000008.quest_desc: ["Sell me one finished Jaffa crate. The registered item is the Jaffa Pallet: 24 boxes and 240 cakes. I pay one Crown (512 exchange value) per shipment, making a properly automated renewable line a strong Era 1 investment." "This contract is repeatable. Claiming it consumes one finished Jaffa Pallet and automatically pays one Numismatics Crown." ]
	quest.5E0000000000001F.title: "The Buried Gate"
	quest.5E0000000000001F.quest_desc: ["Enter the Ancient City containing the reinforced-deepslate gateway." "Objective: enter minecraft:ancient_city. Detection is automatic while standing inside a generated structure piece."]
	chapter_group.569AB980347C1123.title: "Coveted Technology - AE2 and Cyberware"
	chapter_group.4E65FAAC62D57D4A.title: "Civilization Specializations"
	chapter.2DFAD86142B7D28D.title: "Scavenging, Defense and Containment"
	chapter.2DFAD86142B7D28D.subtitle: "Recover the ruins while preventing them from consuming the settlement"

	quest.6301100000000001.title: "Create Re-Automated: Follow the Traces"
	quest.6301100000000001.quest_desc: ["Build the brass-and-electron-tube Trace Finder and use its filters to locate the rare traces that point toward finite ore nodes. This integrates the Traces companion instead of relying on blind excavation." "This is part of the optional Era 3 Re-Automated specialization." ]
	quest.6301100000000002.title: "Create Re-Automated: Diamond Bore"
	quest.6301100000000002.quest_desc: ["Upgrade the proven Era 2 iron drill with a diamond block and precision mechanism. This is an extractor drill head, not a player-held pickaxe and not a substitute for Mining Level 3." "This is part of the optional Era 3 Re-Automated specialization." ]
	quest.6301100000000003.title: "Create Re-Automated: Fluid-Assisted Extraction"
	quest.6301100000000003.quest_desc: ["Construct the brass-cased Advanced Extractor. It consumes a small fluid supply while improving node extraction, so provide a controlled tank and return path before commissioning it." "This is part of the optional Era 3 Re-Automated specialization." ]
	quest.6301100000000004.title: "Create Re-Automated: Base-Metal Bits"
	quest.6301100000000004.quest_desc: ["Operate finite nodes long enough to recover copper, iron, and zinc bits. Compact the bits into raw materials; node extraction supplements mining but does not unlock higher-era ores." "This is part of the optional Era 3 Re-Automated specialization." ]
	quest.6301100000000005.title: "Create Re-Automated: Precious Yield"
	quest.6301100000000005.quest_desc: ["Use the diamond drill on the appropriate nodes and separate precious output from the returned node fragments. Water-assisted extraction and dry extraction remain parallel operating choices." "This is part of the optional Era 3 Re-Automated specialization." ]
	quest.6301100000000006.title: "Create Re-Automated: Assemble a Diamond"
	quest.6301100000000006.quest_desc: ["Run diamond bits through their sequenced assembly into unbaked diamonds, then compact them into finished gems. Producing a batch proves the entire node-to-material route rather than one lucky output." "This is part of the optional Era 3 Re-Automated specialization." ]
	quest.6301100000000007.title: "Create Re-Automated: Nether Nodes"
	quest.6301100000000007.quest_desc: ["Survey a Nether trace, protect the lava-side worksite, and extract quartz bits. Nether nodes require their own fluid and drill choices; do not copy the Overworld installation without reviewing JEI." "This is part of the optional Era 3 Re-Automated specialization." ]
	quest.6301100000000008.title: "Create Re-Automated: Netherite Drill"
	quest.6301100000000008.quest_desc: ["Era 4 material access permits the Netherite Drill upgrade. It is a specialist extractor head for the toughest node work, not an early hand-tool bypass." "This visible continuation is deliberately gated by later-era materials so Re-Automated cannot skip the pack progression." ]
	quest.6301100000000009.title: "Create Re-Automated: Stabilizer"
	quest.6301100000000009.quest_desc: ["After Era 5 automation is established, invest a Nether Star and accumulated fragments in a Stabilizer. Holding it on a node makes that finite node recoverable as a block." "This visible continuation is deliberately gated by later-era materials so Re-Automated cannot skip the pack progression." ]
	quest.630110000000000A.title: "Create Re-Automated: Recover a Stable Node"
	quest.630110000000000A.quest_desc: ["Stabilize and recover one iron node with its remaining-capacity data intact. This objective verifies the actual stabilization mechanic before any infinite-node project begins." "This visible continuation is deliberately gated by later-era materials so Re-Automated cannot skip the pack progression." ]
	quest.630110000000000B.title: "Create Re-Automated: Infinite Iron Works"
	quest.630110000000000B.quest_desc: ["Combine stabilized node infrastructure, fragments, Echo Shards, and a Heavy Core into one Infinite Iron Node. This is a late automation specialization—not a new mining level and not permission to bypass gated ores." "This visible continuation is deliberately gated by later-era materials so Re-Automated cannot skip the pack progression." ]
