	quest.6F01000000000020.title: "INTERFACE INDEX // Field Quest Hardware"
	quest.6F01000000000020.quest_subtitle: "A guide to the physical terminals attached to this network"
	quest.6F01000000000020.quest_desc: [
		"NETWORK RECORD // FTB QUEST HARDWARE"
		"The mobile terminal is only one way to reach the recovery ledger. The same quest network can drive wall displays, material-input terminals, redstone detectors, controlled barriers, and automated reward equipment."
		"Most of these blocks expose or react to quest data; they do not create new progress rules. A task still belongs to the team, and a machine linked to it reports to the same record you see here."
		"This branch is optional. Read it before installing public terminals or interacting with protected settlement hardware."
	]
	task.6F02000000000020.title: "Open the field-interface index"

	quest.6F01000000000021.title: "DISPLAY ARRAY // Task Screens"
	quest.6F01000000000021.quest_subtitle: "One task, several physical display sizes"
	quest.6F01000000000021.quest_desc: [
		"DEVICE CLASS // TASK SCREEN"
		"Task Screens are available in 1×1, 3×3, 5×5, and 7×7 assemblies. Their size changes visibility and installation footprint, not the quest requirement to which they are bound."
		"A configured screen can display a task and, where that task supports physical submission, accept the appropriate items, fluid, or energy through its exposed handlers. Input-only and icon-visibility settings allow pack infrastructure to use the same block as a clean submission port."
		"Large screens are assembled from smaller ones. Consult JEI before committing a wall to the installation; the wall has no vote, but rebuilding it remains your problem."
	]
	task.6F02000000000021.title: "Review Task Screen sizes and submission behavior"

	quest.6F01000000000022.title: "BINDING TOOL // Task Screen Configurator"
	quest.6F01000000000022.quest_subtitle: "Bind a physical terminal to one quest task"
	quest.6F01000000000022.quest_desc: [
		"DEVICE CLASS // CONFIGURATOR"
		"The Task Screen Configurator carries a task binding. Sneak-use it on a Task Screen to apply that binding where your permissions allow. The task index matters when a quest contains several objectives."
		"Do not rebind public settlement terminals merely to see whether you can. A screen pointed at the wrong task can make a functioning intake appear broken while depositing resources into an entirely different contract."
		"Private workshop screens are suitable for experiments. Protected hub equipment is not."
	]
	task.6F02000000000022.title: "Review safe task binding and task-index selection"

	quest.6F01000000000023.title: "SIGNAL OUTPUT // Quest Detectors"
	quest.6F01000000000023.quest_subtitle: "Turn quest state into machinery control"
	quest.6F01000000000023.quest_desc: [
		"DEVICE CLASS // DETECTOR"
		"Quest detectors observe a configured quest object or task and expose its state to the world. Redstone output can authorize doors, start machinery, illuminate status boards, or signal that a team has reached a required recovery stage."
		"Player-detection and notification modes serve different installations. Treat every detector as control wiring: label what it watches, document the expected output, and avoid hiding essential progression behind an unlabeled wall."
		"Configuration generally belongs to pack builders or authorized settlement operators. Ordinary players may encounter these devices without being permitted to alter them."
	]
	task.6F02000000000023.title: "Review quest-state detection and redstone output"

	quest.6F01000000000024.title: "HAZARD CONTROL // Quest and Stage Barriers"
	quest.6F01000000000024.quest_subtitle: "A locked route is a safety system, not an invitation"
	quest.6F01000000000024.quest_desc: [
		"WARNING // CONTROLLED ACCESS"
		"Quest Barriers open when their configured quest condition permits passage. Stage Barriers perform the same duty for a granted progression stage. They may be skinned as another block or become invisible when open."
		"These are infrastructure controls used for containment, tutorials, protected machinery, and staged access. They are normally configured by pack builders, not crafted as ordinary construction material."
		"If a barrier remains closed, inspect the linked requirement in the terminal. Do not mine around a containment system unless I have explicitly identified structural demolition as the objective."
	]
	task.6F02000000000024.title: "Acknowledge controlled-access barrier protocol"

	quest.6F01000000000025.title: "REWARD HANDLING // Loot Crate Equipment"
	quest.6F01000000000025.quest_subtitle: "Open and store network-issued crate rewards"
	quest.6F01000000000025.quest_desc: [
		"DEVICE CLASS // LOOT CRATE HANDLING"
		"Loot crates belong to configured reward tables. The Loot Crate Opener converts stored crates into their contents without requiring you to open every crate by hand; compatible storage equipment can retain crates for later processing."
		"A crate is not a guaranteed specific item unless its reward table says so. It is a sealed allocation from a weighted inventory. Plan around confirmed production, not the optimistic interpretation of a box."
		"Use JEI for the live opener recipe before building an automated reward line."
	]
	task.6F02000000000025.title: "Review loot-crate opening and storage behavior"

	quest.6F01000000000026.title: "FIELD INSTALLATION // Build a Task Screen"
	quest.6F01000000000026.quest_subtitle: "Assemble one local terminal and retain its binding tool"
	quest.6F01000000000026.quest_desc: [
		"INSTALLATION ORDER // ONE-BLOCK TASK SCREEN"
		"Craft a 1×1 Task Screen using the live JEI recipe. The objective detects the screen in your inventory and does not consume it."
		"On completion I will issue one Task Screen Configurator. Use it only on terminals you are authorized to manage. The tool does not grant permission; it merely makes an authorized binding possible."
		"Larger displays remain optional expansions assembled from the smaller screen family."
	]
	task.6F02000000000026.title: "Craft one 1×1 Task Screen"
	// BEGIN GENERATED SPORE THREAT DOSSIER
	chapter_group.5F0A5E0000000001.title: "Persistent Threats"
	chapter.5F0A5E0000000002.title: "The Rot — Spore Threat Dossier"
	chapter.5F0A5E0000000002.subtitle: "Critical containment intelligence // adaptive infection and regional collapse"
	quest.5F10000000000001.title: "The Rot Does Not Wait"
	quest.5F10000000000001.quest_desc: ["Spore is the pack's evolving fungal-infection threat system; this dossier teaches identification and containment." "I had hoped the movement outside was merely another starving corpse. It is not. The tissue is fungal, coordinated, and offensively enthusiastic." "Kill one Infected Human. This dossier never waits for an era unlock because neither does the infection. If this specimen strains your equipment, advance the other quest lines before attempting to be heroic."]
	task.6F00000000010001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Infected Human"
	quest.5F10000000000002.title: "Filter First, Bravado Later"
	quest.5F10000000000002.quest_desc: ["Obtain a Gas Mask and keep it available around contaminated ground. It is equipment, not a certificate of invulnerability—an apparently difficult distinction for armed survivors." "Cold suppresses most Spore organisms. Fire may remove biomass, but relying on one damage method is an excellent way to teach an adaptive predator your habits."]
	task.6F00000000020001.title: "Obtain 1 x Gas Mask"
	quest.5F10000000000003.title: "Still Wearing a Face"
	quest.5F10000000000003.quest_desc: ["Kill six Infected Humans. They retain enough anatomy to be recognizable and enough coordination to make recognition a tactical liability." "Do not let apparently minor infected accumulate kills. Spore organisms use kill points to strengthen themselves and the wider infestation."]
	task.6F00000000030001.title: "Eliminate 6 x Infected Human"
	quest.5F10000000000004.title: "Desiccation Was Not a Cure"
	quest.5F10000000000004.quest_desc: ["Kill four Infected Husks. The fungus has adapted quite comfortably to a host that was already dried out, which is biologically fascinating and aesthetically unforgivable." "Treat every familiar silhouette as unverified until it stops moving."]
	task.6F00000000040001.title: "Eliminate 4 x Infected Husk"
	quest.5F10000000000005.title: "The Water Is Compromised"
	quest.5F10000000000005.quest_desc: ["Kill four Infected Drowned. Aquatic variants mean coastlines and reservoirs are approach routes, not defensive walls." "Inspect water intakes, light submerged access points, and avoid fighting where retreat requires swimming through the same teeth pursuing you."]
	task.6F00000000050001.title: "Eliminate 4 x Infected Drowned"
	quest.5F10000000000006.title: "A Lab Coat Proves Nothing"
	quest.5F10000000000006.quest_desc: ["Kill two Infected Scientists. Apparently education does not confer immunity; it merely gives the Rot better pockets." "Search laboratories cautiously. Infested rooms, growth blocks, and spawners can sustain an outbreak after the visible occupants are dead."]
	task.6F00000000060001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Infected Scientist"
	quest.5F10000000000007.title: "First Tissue Submission"
	quest.5F10000000000007.quest_desc: ["Submit four Preserved Infected Tissue samples. Yes, I want them sealed. No, your ordinary lunch container does not become a laboratory vessel because you wiped it on your sleeve." "The Charger and Biomonitor are advance compensation. You may not yet possess the infrastructure to use or install them; store them safely instead of improvising surgery."]
	task.6F00000000070001.title: "Submit 4 x Preserved Infected Tissue"
	quest.5F10000000000008.title: "The Rot Has Inventory"
	quest.5F10000000000008.quest_desc: ["Collect Biomass, Tumors, and Mutated Fibre. These are not trophies. They are evidence that the infection manufactures specialized tissue instead of merely consuming hosts." "Keep samples isolated from food stores and living soil. That sentence should have been unnecessary, yet here we are."]
	task.6F00000000080001.title: "Obtain 32 x Biomass"
	task.6F00000000080002.title: "Obtain 8 x Tumor"
	task.6F00000000080003.title: "Obtain 8 x Mutated Fibre"
	quest.5F10000000000009.title: "Knight: The Fungus Discovers Armor"
	quest.5F10000000000009.quest_desc: ["Kill four Knights. Their reinforced bodies prove the Rot can specialize for frontal assault." "If you thought the infected were unpleasant, congratulations: those were the organisms before they began allocating a budget."]
	task.6F00000000090001.title: "Eliminate 4 x Knight"
	quest.5F1000000000000A.title: "Spitter: Distance Is Not Safety"
	quest.5F1000000000000A.quest_desc: ["Kill four Spitters. Break line of sight, use cover, and do not cluster where one projectile can contaminate an entire firing position." "The creature has converted digestion into artillery. I am impressed by the efficiency and disgusted by every other part of that sentence."]
	task.6F000000000A0001.title: "Eliminate 4 x Spitter"
	quest.5F1000000000000B.title: "Howler: An Alarm With Organs"
	quest.5F1000000000000B.quest_desc: ["Kill three Howlers. Prioritize them before they turn a manageable contact into a coordinated response." "Spore mobs can share targets through links and signals. The loud one is not merely being theatrical, though I resent the competition."]
	task.6F000000000B0001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Howler"
	quest.5F1000000000000C.title: "Stalker: Check the Ceiling"
	quest.5F1000000000000C.quest_desc: ["Kill three Stalkers. Sweep above doors, behind machinery, and across vertical surfaces before entering a contaminated room." "If you thought the Howler was bad, this one has discovered patience. You might consider doing the same."]
	task.6F000000000C0001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Stalker"
	quest.5F1000000000000D.title: "Brute: Apply More Planning"
	quest.5F1000000000000D.quest_desc: ["Kill two Brutes. Do not trade blows merely to demonstrate that your skeleton is technically present." "Use obstacles, ranged fire, cold effects, and a retreat lane. Your weapon is only one component of the solution."]
	task.6F000000000D0001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Brute"
	quest.5F1000000000000E.title: "Gorgon: Biology Becomes a Weapon System"
	quest.5F1000000000000E.quest_desc: ["Kill one Gorgon. This is no longer an infected animal improvising violence; it is a purpose-built organism." "If you thought the Brute was bad, the next ranks abandon recognizable anatomy almost entirely. Improve your equipment while you still have the option."]
	task.6F000000000E0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Gorgon"
	quest.5F1000000000000F.title: "Evolved Mutagen Submission"
	quest.5F1000000000000F.quest_desc: ["Submit six Evolved Mutagen Samples. I can now compare specialization across multiple combat forms without asking you to carry an entire twitching carcass home." "The storage cell and targeting implant are field-research dividends. The implant still requires proper surgery. I refuse to debug your skull with a wrench."]
	task.6F000000000F0001.title: "Submit 6 x Evolved Mutagen Sample"
	quest.5F10000000000010.title: "Specialized Anatomy"
	quest.5F10000000000010.quest_desc: ["Collect Hypersuspensile Ligaments, Alveolic Sacks, Spikes, and Wing Membranes. The Rot has solved locomotion, respiration, armor penetration, and flight using wet components grown to order." "Interesting, yes. Touching any of it without gloves remains stupid."]
	task.6F00000000100001.title: "Obtain 8 x Hypersuspensile Ligaments"
	task.6F00000000100002.title: "Obtain 4 x Alveolic Sack"
	task.6F00000000100003.title: "Obtain 8 x Spike"
	task.6F00000000100004.title: "Obtain 4 x Wing Membrane"
	quest.5F10000000000011.title: "Inquisitor: It Has Opinions"
	quest.5F10000000000011.quest_desc: ["Kill two Inquisitors. Hyper-evolved forms combine durability, reach, and tactical behavior rather than merely increasing mass." "If it appears to be judging your tactics, improve them. I dislike conceding intellectual ground to a walking fungal indictment."]
	task.6F00000000110001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Inquisitor"
	quest.5F10000000000012.title: "Wendigo: Speed With Too Many Joints"
	quest.5F10000000000012.quest_desc: ["Kill two Wendigos. Maintain overlapping fire and deny it an isolated target." "A lone survivor is prey; a prepared team is a geometry problem. Try to be the latter."]
	task.6F00000000120001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Wendigo"
	quest.5F10000000000013.title: "Ogre: Structural Damage Is an Attack"
	quest.5F10000000000013.quest_desc: ["Kill one Ogre. Fight away from irreplaceable machines, weak walls, and the room containing every resource you own." "Your base layout is now part of combat doctrine. Four decorative blocks and optimism do not constitute fortification."]
	task.6F00000000130001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Ogre"
	quest.5F10000000000014.title: "Brotkatze: Ambush Predator"
	quest.5F10000000000014.quest_desc: ["Kill one Brotkatze. Watch flanks, maintain illumination, and do not pursue it into terrain you have not cleared." "If you thought the Ogre was bad, this one wastes less mass and considerably less time."]
	task.6F00000000140001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Brotkatze"
	quest.5F10000000000015.title: "Hyper-Evolved Core Submission"
	quest.5F10000000000015.quest_desc: ["Submit four Hyper-Evolved Core Samples. Their internal organization is revoltingly elegant; multiple specialized tissues behave like replaceable machine modules." "I am issuing a larger storage cell and Wired Reflexes. Have a competent surgeon install the latter. Competence is not implied by ownership of a sharp object."]
	task.6F00000000150001.title: "Submit 4 x Hyper-Evolved Core Sample"
	quest.5F10000000000016.title: "Armor, Cores, and Spines"
	quest.5F10000000000016.quest_desc: ["Collect Armor Plates, Living Cores, Hardened Binds, and Spine Segments. These tissues explain why late organisms shrug off improvised weapons." "Spore creatures are generally vulnerable to cold. Vary damage methods and keep cryogenic tools available; adaptation rewards repetition, including repetitive mistakes."]
	task.6F00000000160001.title: "Obtain 8 x Armor Plate"
	task.6F00000000160002.title: "Obtain 4 x Living Core"
	task.6F00000000160003.title: "Obtain 8 x Hardened Bind"
	task.6F00000000160004.title: "Obtain 8 x Spine Segment"
	quest.5F10000000000017.title: "Flesh Mound: An Outpost That Breathes"
	quest.5F10000000000017.quest_desc: ["Kill three Flesh Mounds. They are infrastructure: persistent biological outposts that support spread and nearby organisms." "Destroy the organism and clear its growths. Leaving the infected terrain intact is gardening for an enemy that already considers you fertilizer."]
	task.6F00000000170001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Flesh Mound"
	quest.5F10000000000018.title: "Vigil: The Outpost Has Eyes"
	quest.5F10000000000018.quest_desc: ["Kill one Vigil. Organoids divide battlefield functions between bodies; this one performs observation and coordination." "Remove watchers before assaulting a nest. Being seen is sometimes unavoidable. Remaining seen is usually laziness."]
	task.6F00000000180001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Vigil"
	quest.5F10000000000019.title: "Womb: Reinforcements Manufactured Locally"
	quest.5F10000000000019.quest_desc: ["Kill one Womb. It turns occupied ground into a supply line for new bodies." "Do not farm it casually. Any strategy containing the phrase 'infinite monsters might be useful' has already failed its safety review."]
	task.6F00000000190001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Womb"
	quest.5F1000000000001A.title: "Usurper: The Ground Is Participating"
	quest.5F1000000000001A.quest_desc: ["Kill one Usurper. Organoids can emerge through vulnerable terrain, which makes floor construction a defensive system." "Use hard materials and avoid thick masses of weak blocks in protected interiors. Yes, even the floor requires engineering now."]
	task.6F000000001A0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Usurper"
	quest.5F1000000000001B.title: "Organoid Neural Submission"
	quest.5F1000000000001B.quest_desc: ["Submit four Organoid Neural Samples. Their signal tissue confirms that local bodies can act as one distributed hunting system." "The Wireless Terminal and Neural Processor are appropriate rewards: one extends your network, the other may eventually improve yours. Do not confuse the two during installation."]
	task.6F000000001B0001.title: "Submit 4 x Organoid Neural Sample"
	quest.5F1000000000001C.title: "Organoid Anatomy"
	quest.5F1000000000001C.quest_desc: ["Collect Organoid Membranes, a Vigil Eye, and Cerebrums. The samples show transmission tissue, sensory specialization, and decentralized control." "If Madness appears without a visible attacker, assume a major coordinating organism is nearby. Milky Sacks can remove it; distance and extermination remain preferable."]
	task.6F000000001C0001.title: "Obtain 8 x Organoid Membrane"
	task.6F000000001C0002.title: "Obtain 1 x Eye of the Vigil"
	task.6F000000001C0003.title: "Obtain 4 x Cerebrum"
	quest.5F1000000000001D.title: "Sieger: The Wall Is a Suggestion"
	quest.5F1000000000001D.quest_desc: ["Kill one Sieger. Calamities are siege organisms, not oversized wildlife." "Evacuate noncombatants, establish fallback positions, and fight somewhere you can afford to lose. If you thought the organoids were bad, they were merely preparing the battlefield."]
	task.6F000000001D0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Sieger"
	quest.5F1000000000001E.title: "Howitzer: Counter-Battery Required"
	quest.5F1000000000001E.quest_desc: ["Kill one Howitzer. Break its line of fire and approach through covered routes instead of sprinting across open ground with admirable confidence and no surviving plan." "Long-range biological artillery means towers and rooftops need overhead protection, not just walls."]
	task.6F000000001E0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Howitzer"
	quest.5F1000000000001F.title: "Hohlfresser: Underground Is Not Safe"
	quest.5F1000000000001F.quest_desc: ["Kill one Hohlfresser. Burrowing calamities invalidate the comforting fiction that several metres of dirt make a secure bunker." "Segment underground facilities, harden floors, and maintain more than one exit. A single tunnel is a coffin with civil engineering paperwork."]
	task.6F000000001F0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Hohlfresser"
	quest.5F10000000000020.title: "Gazenbreacher: Do Not Admire It Up Close"
	quest.5F10000000000020.quest_desc: ["Kill one Gazenbreacher. Keep distance, rotate damage sources, and preserve a clear retreat corridor." "Its anatomy is extraordinary. I would enjoy studying it considerably more if it were not trying to study your interior anatomy in return."]
	task.6F00000000200001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Gazenbreacher"
	quest.5F10000000000021.title: "Hindenburg: The Sky Is Infected"
	quest.5F10000000000021.quest_desc: ["Kill one Hindenburg. Airspace is now part of the containment perimeter." "Use ranged weapons, protected firing positions, and redundant access to roofs. Looking upward after the first impact is technically an observation method, just not a good one."]
	task.6F00000000210001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Hindenburg"
	quest.5F10000000000022.title: "Leviathan: The Sea Is Also Infected"
	quest.5F10000000000022.quest_desc: ["Kill one Leviathan. Coastal travel and offshore industry require escort, sonar-by-any-other-name, and an emergency route back to land." "If you thought the Hindenburg was bad, the Rot has also decided oceans contain insufficient nightmares."]
	task.6F00000000220001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Leviathan"
	quest.5F10000000000023.title: "Verfalldrache: Terminal Morphology"
	quest.5F10000000000023.quest_desc: ["Kill one Verfalldrache. This is the infection expressing scale, flight, armor, and predation as a single argument against complacency." "Do not engage because the quest is visible. Engage when the settlement can absorb casualties, equipment loss, and structural damage without collapsing."]
	task.6F00000000230001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Verfalldrache"
	quest.5F10000000000024.title: "Calamity Biomass Submission"
	quest.5F10000000000024.quest_desc: ["Submit five Calamity Biomass Samples. I am running out of polite anatomical terminology, which is a remarkable achievement on the organism's part." "The Dense Energy Cell and Dense Battery reward sustained preparation. Neither will save someone who mistakes stored power for tactical judgment."]
	task.6F00000000240001.title: "Submit 5 x Calamity Biomass Sample"
	quest.5F10000000000025.title: "Three Environments, One Appetite"
	quest.5F10000000000025.quest_desc: ["Collect Terrestrial, Aquatic, and Airborne Reforged Biomass plus an Amalgamated Heart. The Rot does not merely occupy environments; it builds bodies specifically for each of them." "We have enough evidence. What remains is the voice coordinating the evidence into an army."]
	task.6F00000000250001.title: "Obtain 2 x Terrestrial Reforged Biomass"
	task.6F00000000250002.title: "Obtain 2 x Aquatic Reforged Biomass"
	task.6F00000000250003.title: "Obtain 2 x Airborne Reforged Biomass"
	task.6F00000000250004.title: "Obtain 1 x Amalgamated Heart"
	quest.5F10000000000026.title: "Murder the Hive Mind"
	quest.5F10000000000026.quest_desc: ["Kill one Proto Hivemind and submit its Cerebral Sample. It links lesser organisms, spreads Madness across a wide area, and turns scattered growth into coordinated territory." "Destroy supporting organoids first, establish a hardened perimeter, bring cold and varied damage, and plan extraction before contact. If this objective looks premature, it is. Go become less premature." "Once it is dead, give me the sample. I am intrigued, disgusted, and—against my better instincts—quite proud that you survived long enough to make those feelings relevant."]
	task.6F00000000260001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Proto Hivemind"
	task.6F00000000260002.title: "Submit 1 x Hive Mind Cerebral Sample"
	// END GENERATED SPORE THREAT DOSSIER
	// BEGIN GENERATED MUTANT AND MEKANITE THREAT DOSSIER
	chapter.5F0A5E0000000003.title: "Aberrant and Mekanite Threat Determinations"
	chapter.5F0A5E0000000003.subtitle: "Hostile mutation records // identification, escalation, and response"
	quest.5F20000000000001.title: "Mutation Inside the Perimeter"
	quest.5F20000000000001.quest_desc: ["Mutant Monsters adds oversized variants of familiar hostiles with distinct attacks and death behavior." "This is not the Rot. It is ordinary hostile anatomy subjected to an extraordinary and deeply irresponsible increase in mass." "Kill one Mutant Zombie. These mutants have been authorized to spawn inside the initial ring, so this branch is available immediately. Visibility is not a recommendation to fight one with a stone hatchet."]
	task.6F20000000010001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Zombie"
	quest.5F20000000000002.title: "Evaluation: Repeated Resurrection"
	quest.5F20000000000002.quest_desc: ["Kill three Mutant Zombies and observe the collapse sequence. A fallen specimen can rise again unless you finish the work correctly." "When it drops, set the body alight. Standing beside it and hoping that death has become permanent is not a containment protocol."]
	task.6F20000000020001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Mutant Zombie"
	quest.5F20000000000003.title: "Evaluation: Articulated Ballistics"
	quest.5F20000000000003.quest_desc: ["Kill a Mutant Skeleton. Its ranged attacks and detachable anatomy make open ground a particularly educational place to die." "Use hard cover, close distance deliberately, and expect the remains to stay tactically relevant after the central body fails."]
	task.6F20000000030001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Skeleton"
	quest.5F20000000000004.title: "Evaluation: Explosive Regeneration"
	quest.5F20000000000004.quest_desc: ["Kill a Mutant Creeper. Distance, line-of-sight breaks, and terrain you can afford to lose are the minimum requirements." "Its death sequence is not permission to approach the crater. You have survived long enough that I should not need to explain secondary explosions, yet here we are."]
	task.6F20000000040001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Creeper"
	quest.5F20000000000005.title: "Evaluation: Hostile Geometry"
	quest.5F20000000000005.quest_desc: ["Kill a Mutant Enderman. It teleports, throws terrain, produces Endersoul Clones, and generally treats distance as a suggestion." "Fight beneath controlled cover, clear loose blocks from the position, and stop staring at empty space after it relocates. It has not become polite; it has moved."]
	task.6F20000000050001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Enderman"
	quest.5F20000000000006.title: "Zombie Termination Procedure"
	quest.5F20000000000006.quest_desc: ["Repeat the engagement and recover a Hulk Hammer. The tool confirms terminal tissue failure and is substantially more convincing than your verbal assurance that the corpse looked finished." "The hammer is detected but not consumed. Keep it available; blunt-force redundancy is one of the few redundancies nobody complains about during an attack."]
	task.6F20000000060001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Zombie"
	task.6F20000000060002.title: "Obtain 1 x Hulk Hammer"
	quest.5F20000000000007.title: "Skeleton Recovery Drill"
	quest.5F20000000000007.quest_desc: ["Kill two Mutant Skeletons. Separate their firing lane from the rest of the battlefield instead of allowing every hostile creature to participate in the same experiment." "Recoverable skeletal components are useful. They are still evidence from an armed corpse, not tasteful interior decoration."]
	task.6F20000000070001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Mutant Skeleton"
	quest.5F20000000000008.title: "Creeper Containment Drill"
	quest.5F20000000000008.quest_desc: ["Kill two Mutant Creepers without conducting the test beside the settlement wall, fuel depot, animal pens, or anything else you were hoping to retain." "Control the battlefield first. Damage output is not impressive when the enemy chooses what your weapon destroys."]
	task.6F20000000080001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Mutant Creeper"
	quest.5F20000000000009.title: "Endersoul Containment Drill"
	quest.5F20000000000009.quest_desc: ["Kill two Mutant Endermen. Mark the original target and do not waste ammunition proving that an Endersoul Clone can disappear." "A low roof limits thrown blocks and vertical displacement. It will not make the encounter easy; it merely replaces chaos with a problem you can solve."]
	task.6F20000000090001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Mutant Enderman"
	quest.5F2000000000000A.title: "Determination: Mutant-Class Threat"
	quest.5F2000000000000A.quest_desc: ["Eliminate one of each naturally occurring mutant class after completing the individual evaluations. The conclusion is refreshingly uncomplicated: they are independent apex contacts, not a coordinated ecology." "Maintain separate procedures for resurrection, artillery, blast radius, and teleportation. Calling all four 'the large one' is concise but strategically useless."]
	task.6F200000000A0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Zombie"
	task.6F200000000A0002.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Skeleton"
	task.6F200000000A0003.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Creeper"
	task.6F200000000A0004.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Enderman"
	quest.5F2000000000000B.title: "Controlled Mutation: Snow Golem"
	quest.5F2000000000000B.quest_desc: ["Create and then defeat a Mutant Snow Golem with Chemical X. This is an optional controlled trial, though 'controlled' is carrying an heroic amount of meaning." "Perform it away from the hub and anything flammable. Manufactured threats do not become less embarrassing because the laboratory form was signed correctly."]
	task.6F200000000B0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mutant Snow Golem"
	quest.5F2000000000000C.title: "Controlled Mutation: Spider Pig"
	quest.5F2000000000000C.quest_desc: ["Create and defeat a Spider Pig with Chemical X. Yes, the name is accurate. No, the result is not improved by being funny." "Use a contained test ground and preserve an exit. Combining porcine persistence with arachnid movement was not a request civilization needed answered."]
	task.6F200000000C0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Spider Pig"
	quest.5F2000000000000D.title: "Northern Contact: Machines in the Treeline"
	quest.5F2000000000000D.quest_desc: ["Mekanite Mobs supplies the late-game machine hostiles in the north, Cyberspace, and the Darknet. The northern normal biomes contain hostiles that are mechanical in construction and biological only by analogy; they do not occur in the starting ring." "After reaching Era 8 and completing the northern survey, destroy one Drone. If this machine feels unfair, that is because you brought early-era assumptions to an endgame weapons platform."]
	task.6F200000000D0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Drone"
	quest.5F2000000000000E.title: "Southern Contact: Armored Desiccation"
	quest.5F2000000000000E.quest_desc: ["The southern deserts and badlands host Mekanite Husks. Cross the ocean only after the Era 8 logistics chain can support extraction as well as arrival." "Destroy one Mekanite Zombie Husk. Heat management, ranged fire, and a marked return route are equipment, not optional mood-setting."]
	task.6F200000000E0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Zombie Husk"
	quest.5F2000000000000F.title: "Ocean Contact: Electrified Boarding Party"
	quest.5F2000000000000F.quest_desc: ["Cold and deep oceans contain Mekanite Zombie Drowned. Their habitat makes a damaged vessel, flooded compartment, or interrupted air supply part of the encounter." "Destroy one only after Era 8 and the northern ocean survey. Fighting underwater without an extraction system is merely drowning with additional paperwork."]
	task.6F200000000F0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Zombie Drowned"
	quest.5F20000000000010.title: "Northern Line Infantry"
	quest.5F20000000000010.quest_desc: ["Destroy three Mekanite Zombies in forest, plains, taiga, swamp, jungle, beach, savanna, or dark forest terrain." "Do not mistake a familiar silhouette for familiar durability. Their components turn a basic melee profile into an industrial accident with legs."]
	task.6F20000000100001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Mekanite Zombie"
	quest.5F20000000000011.title: "Ballistic Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000011.quest_desc: ["Destroy three Mekanite Skeletons. Their common habitat overlaps the Zombie patrol zones, so assume combined contacts rather than arranging a courteous duel." "Break line of sight, isolate firing angles, and close only when the route is actually clear. Running directly at a gun remains a poor innovation."]
	task.6F20000000110001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Mekanite Skeleton"
	quest.5F20000000000012.title: "Chemical Warfare Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000012.quest_desc: ["Destroy two Mekanite Witches in forested, frozen-spike, jungle, mushroom, or swamp terrain." "Carry cleansing supplies and fight from positions that let status effects expire without allowing the rest of the biome to join in."]
	task.6F20000000120001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Mekanite Witch"
	quest.5F20000000000013.title: "Decoy Command Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000013.quest_desc: ["Destroy two Mekanite Illusioners. Their clones are projections of the encounter, not a separate wildlife population, so the terminal records the actual chassis." "Track the source, use cover against ranged fire, and resist the urge to attack every identical silhouette in alphabetical order."]
	task.6F20000000130001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Mekanite Illusioner"
	quest.5F20000000000014.title: "Northern Heavy Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000014.quest_desc: ["Destroy one Mekanite Ravager in taiga, savanna, forest, or dark forest terrain." "Establish obstacles, overlapping fire, and a retreat route before contact. A large target is not automatically an easy target; thank you for attending this advanced geometry lecture."]
	task.6F20000000140001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Ravager"
	quest.5F20000000000015.title: "Southern Demolition Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000015.quest_desc: ["Destroy three Mekanite Creepers. Their reinforced construction turns blast management into an infrastructure requirement." "Fight beyond the expedition camp and never beside the vessel that must carry you home. This distinction is why I retain custody of the maps."]
	task.6F20000000150001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Mekanite Creeper"
	quest.5F20000000000016.title: "Electrified Web Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000016.quest_desc: ["Destroy four Mekanite Spiders across the warm outer biomes. Their mobility makes open, illuminated firing lanes more useful than an ornate camp perimeter." "Watch vertical surfaces and remove webs before they turn your withdrawal route into an exhibit on poor planning."]
	task.6F20000000160001.title: "Eliminate 4 x Mekanite Spider"
	quest.5F20000000000017.title: "Assault Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000017.quest_desc: ["Destroy three Mekanite Vindicators in plains, forests, taiga, savanna, or savanna plateau terrain." "Their close-range pressure is designed to punish a scattered formation. Maintain spacing without becoming isolated—an elementary distinction under regrettably non-elementary conditions."]
	task.6F20000000170001.title: "Eliminate 3 x Mekanite Vindicator"
	quest.5F20000000000018.title: "Self-Dividing Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000018.quest_desc: ["Destroy a complete Mekanite Slime hierarchy: Big, Medium, and Small. The smaller chassis are still part of the threat, not debris." "Control the surrounding ground before splitting the largest body. Multiplication is less charming when every result is armed."]
	task.6F20000000180001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Big Slime"
	task.6F20000000180002.title: "Eliminate 2 x Mekanite Medium Slime"
	task.6F20000000180003.title: "Eliminate 4 x Mekanite Small Slime"
	quest.5F20000000000019.title: "Displacement Chassis"
	quest.5F20000000000019.quest_desc: ["Destroy two Mekanite Endermen. They appear across select northern, southern, coastal, Nether, End, Cyberspace, and Darknet biomes, because ordinary geographic restraint was apparently beneath their designers." "Use overhead cover and redundant targeting. If your plan depends upon the target remaining where you first saw it, you have described a wish."]
	task.6F20000000190001.title: "Eliminate 2 x Mekanite Enderman"
	quest.5F2000000000001A.title: "Determination: Mekanite Extermination Doctrine"
	quest.5F2000000000001A.quest_desc: ["The outer continents, Cyberspace, and the Darknet support a distributed weapons ecology: patrol, artillery, demolition, chemical, decoy, displacement, aquatic, dividing, and heavy assault chassis." "Destroy the representative command threats and return alive. The determination is final: these are Era 8 expedition hazards. They are not an exotic source of early salvage and the ocean is not a shortcut around progression."]
	task.6F200000001A0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Ravager"
	task.6F200000001A0002.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Vindicator"
	task.6F200000001A0003.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Enderman"
	task.6F200000001A0004.title: "Eliminate 1 x Mekanite Zombie Drowned"
	// END GENERATED MUTANT AND MEKANITE THREAT DOSSIER
	// BEGIN GENERATED DARKNET DRACONIC CONVERGENCE
	chapter.381AB56C38F92B74.title: "Darknet Draconic Convergence"
	chapter.381AB56C38F92B74.subtitle: "Classified network record // draconic ecology beyond ordinary infrastructure"
	task.6B10000000010001.title: "Obtain 1 x Netcracker"
	quest.5B10000000000001.title: "A Less Reputable Connection"
	quest.5B10000000000001.quest_desc: ["Acquire a Netcracker. Open the nearby Terminal's inventory and place the Netcracker in its hardware slot; the ordinary Cyberspace link will expose a Darknet connection while it remains installed." "Yes, the illegal-looking cartridge goes into the conspicuously empty computer slot. The design is not subtle. It merely had the decency to omit a manual."]
	task.6B10000000020001.title: "Enter Darknet"
	quest.5B10000000000002.title: "One Hundred Seconds of Bad Decisions"
	quest.5B10000000000002.quest_desc: ["Select the Darknet connection in the Terminal. The transfer takes two seconds. Your first connection lands at a random Darknet position; later connections remember the last Darknet coordinates." "A 100-second countdown begins on arrival. When it expires, the system forcibly returns you to the Overworld coordinates recorded when the connection started. Do not move the Terminal, obstruct the return point, or confuse a timer with an invitation to sightsee." "The Darknet is now occupied by Mekanite war machines and all three draconic species. Arrive armored, carry ranged damage, and plan what can actually be accomplished inside five thousand ticks."]
	task.6B10000000030001.title: "Obtain 1 x Data Extractor"
	task.6B10000000030002.title: "Obtain 1 x Data Hardware"
	quest.5B10000000000003.title: "Darknet Data Extraction"
	quest.5B10000000000003.quest_desc: ["Install a Data Extractor in the same Terminal hardware slot when you intend to recover data rather than open the Darknet link. Bring back Data Hardware as proof that the trip produced something besides elevated pulse rate." "The slot accepts one specialist tool at a time. Swap deliberately; staring at the absent Darknet command while the wrong module is installed will not improve the interface."]
	task.6B10000000040001.title: "Obtain 1 x Riftmaker"
	task.6B10000000040002.title: "Complete a timed Darknet incursion and return alive"
	quest.5B10000000000004.title: "Return Before the Carrier Drops"
	quest.5B10000000000004.quest_desc: ["Complete one Darknet incursion and return alive. Falling below elevation 48 imposes Darkness, although the dimension suppresses fall distance; neither feature makes the lower void a sensible extraction route." "The timer is the reliable exit. The default Leave Cyberspace key is for Cyberspace; do not build a Darknet plan around an exit control that the Darknet session already replaces with forced recall."]
	task.6B10000000050001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Fire Dragon"
	quest.5B10000000000005.title: "Fire Signature in the Dark"
	quest.5B10000000000005.quest_desc: ["Ice and Fire supplies the dragons, trophies, materials, and Dragonforge industry encountered in this campaign." "Kill a Fire Dragon in the Darknet. Treat the flat horizon as a firing lane for both parties and remember that the countdown continues while you admire the target." "Wild dragons are not tameable. If you want one that obeys, you will need an egg from a high-stage female and the patience to raise what hatches."]
	task.6B10000000060001.title: "Obtain 1 x Fire Dragon Heart"
	task.6B10000000060002.title: "Obtain 1 x Fire Dragon Blood"
	task.6B10000000060003.title: "Obtain 4 x Fire Dragon Flesh"
	task.6B10000000060004.title: "Obtain 1 x Fire Dragon Skull"
	task.6B10000000060005.title: "Obtain 16 x Dragon Bone"
	task.6B10000000060006.title: "Obtain 8 x Red Dragon Scales"
	quest.5B10000000000006.title: "Fire Dragon Specimens"
	quest.5B10000000000006.quest_desc: ["Recover the heart, blood, flesh, skull, bones, and red scales from the corpse. Loot a fallen dragon by interacting with its body; waiting for it to behave like an ordinary item fountain is charmingly optimistic."]
	task.6B10000000070001.title: "Obtain 17 x Fire Dragonforge Brick"
	task.6B10000000070002.title: "Obtain 1 x Fire Dragonforge Core"
	task.6B10000000070003.title: "Obtain 1 x Fire Dragonforge Input"
	quest.5B10000000000007.title: "Fire Dragonforge Plant"
	quest.5B10000000000007.quest_desc: ["Construct the active components for a Fire Dragonforge: seventeen Fire Dragonforge Bricks, one Fire Dragonforge Core, and one Fire Dragonforge Input. The assembled forge must receive breath from a Stage 2 or older Fire Dragon." "This is a multiblock industrial furnace powered by a living siege weapon. Give the breath path clearance and stop calling the animal a fuel line where it can hear you."]
	task.6B10000000080001.title: "Obtain 4 x Fire Dragonsteel Ingot"
	quest.5B10000000000008.title: "Fire Dragonsteel"
	quest.5B10000000000008.quest_desc: ["Use the completed Fire Dragonforge to produce four Fire Dragonsteel Ingots. The dragon supplies the breath; the forge supplies containment; your contribution is keeping both pointed at the correct aperture."]
	task.6B10000000090001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Ice Dragon"
	quest.5B10000000000009.title: "Ice Signature in the Dark"
	quest.5B10000000000009.quest_desc: ["Kill an Ice Dragon in the Darknet. Cover remains useful until the breath freezes the terrain around it, at which point your carefully selected position becomes a sculpture commemorating misplaced confidence."]
	task.6B100000000A0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Ice Dragon Heart"
	task.6B100000000A0002.title: "Obtain 1 x Ice Dragon Blood"
	task.6B100000000A0003.title: "Obtain 4 x Ice Dragon Flesh"
	task.6B100000000A0004.title: "Obtain 1 x Ice Dragon Skull"
	task.6B100000000A0005.title: "Obtain 16 x Dragon Bone"
	task.6B100000000A0006.title: "Obtain 8 x Blue Dragon Scales"
	quest.5B1000000000000A.title: "Ice Dragon Specimens"
	quest.5B1000000000000A.quest_desc: ["Recover the heart, blood, flesh, skull, bones, and blue scales. The elemental material is the technological point of this expedition; the enormous corpse was not killed merely to improve your decorating options."]
	task.6B100000000B0001.title: "Obtain 17 x Ice Dragonforge Brick"
	task.6B100000000B0002.title: "Obtain 1 x Ice Dragonforge Core"
	task.6B100000000B0003.title: "Obtain 1 x Ice Dragonforge Input"
	quest.5B1000000000000B.title: "Ice Dragonforge Plant"
	quest.5B1000000000000B.quest_desc: ["Construct seventeen Ice Dragonforge Bricks, one Ice Dragonforge Core, and one Ice Dragonforge Input. A Stage 2 or older Ice Dragon must breathe into the input to operate the assembled forge." "Water management belongs outside the breath channel. Freezing the workshop floor is not a refrigeration system; it is a staffing problem."]
	task.6B100000000C0001.title: "Obtain 4 x Ice Dragonsteel Ingot"
	quest.5B1000000000000C.title: "Ice Dragonsteel"
	quest.5B1000000000000C.quest_desc: ["Use the completed Ice Dragonforge to produce four Ice Dragonsteel Ingots. If the dragon is present but the forge is idle, inspect the multiblock and breath alignment before accusing a reptile of poor process control."]
	task.6B100000000D0001.title: "Eliminate 1 x Lightning Dragon"
	quest.5B1000000000000D.title: "Lightning Signature in the Dark"
	quest.5B1000000000000D.quest_desc: ["Kill a Lightning Dragon in the Darknet. Spread out, avoid conductive clutter, and do not mistake a flat arena for safety when the target's preferred geometry is a bolt from above."]
	task.6B100000000E0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Lightning Dragon Heart"
	task.6B100000000E0002.title: "Obtain 1 x Lightning Dragon Blood"
	task.6B100000000E0003.title: "Obtain 4 x Lightning Dragon Flesh"
	task.6B100000000E0004.title: "Obtain 1 x Lightning Dragon Skull"
	task.6B100000000E0005.title: "Obtain 16 x Dragon Bone"
	task.6B100000000E0006.title: "Obtain 8 x Electric Dragon Scales"
	quest.5B1000000000000E.title: "Lightning Dragon Specimens"
	quest.5B1000000000000E.quest_desc: ["Recover the heart, blood, flesh, skull, bones, and electric-blue scales. Keep the samples isolated until the laboratory has earned the right to discover which storage cabinet conducts electricity."]
	task.6B100000000F0001.title: "Obtain 17 x Lightning Dragonforge Brick"
	task.6B100000000F0002.title: "Obtain 1 x Lightning Dragonforge Core"
	task.6B100000000F0003.title: "Obtain 1 x Lightning Dragonforge Input"
	quest.5B1000000000000F.title: "Lightning Dragonforge Plant"
	quest.5B1000000000000F.quest_desc: ["Construct seventeen Lightning Dragonforge Bricks, one Lightning Dragonforge Core, and one Lightning Dragonforge Input. Power the completed forge with the breath of a Stage 2 or older Lightning Dragon." "Ground the surrounding installation. 'It only arcs when operating' is a diagnosis, not a safety certification."]
	task.6B10000000100001.title: "Obtain 4 x Lightning Dragonsteel Ingot"
	quest.5B10000000000010.title: "Lightning Dragonsteel"
	quest.5B10000000000010.quest_desc: ["Use the completed Lightning Dragonforge to produce four Lightning Dragonsteel Ingots. Congratulations: the lightning-breathing apex predator is now a qualified metallurgical subprocess."]
	task.6B10000000110001.title: "Obtain a Dragon Egg"
	quest.5B10000000000011.title: "An Egg Is Not Salvage"
	quest.5B10000000000011.quest_desc: ["Recover a Dragon Egg from a Stage 4 or Stage 5 female. The species and color may vary; the important distinction is that an egg is a future tamed dragon, not another crafting component to leave in an unsorted chest."]
	task.6B10000000120001.title: "Obtain 8 x Dragon Meal"
	task.6B10000000120002.title: "Hatch and bond with a Dragon"
	quest.5B10000000000012.title: "Incubation Is Elemental"
	quest.5B10000000000012.quest_desc: ["Hatch the egg under the condition matching its species. Fire eggs remain in fire; Ice eggs remain in water until it freezes; Lightning eggs require open sky and active rain. Hatching takes several minutes and pauses if the condition fails." "Stay nearby. A hatchling bonds to the nearby player as it emerges. Lightning incubation can ignite its surroundings, so keep water available unless your nursery plan includes an electrical fire." "Prepare Dragon Meal as well. Each meal advances growth by one day; Stage 3 is the threshold for riding, not a reason to force-feed seventy-five portions in one sitting."]
	task.6B10000000130001.title: "Obtain 1 x Dragon Command Staff"
	task.6B10000000130002.title: "Obtain 1 x Dragon Bone Flute"
	task.6B10000000130003.title: "Obtain 1 x Dragon Horn"
	quest.5B10000000000013.title: "Command, Recall, and Storage"
	quest.5B10000000000013.quest_desc: ["Equip the basic husbandry set. The Dragon Command Staff changes behavior and sets a home position while sneaking. The Dragon Bone Flute calls a flying dragon down. The Dragon Horn stores and releases your own dragon for transport." "Use the tools before trusting a growing dragon near machinery. Ownership is not the same thing as operational discipline, a distinction many managers also fail to grasp."]
	task.6B10000000140001.title: "Raise and ride a Stage 3 bonded Dragon"
	task.6B10000000140002.title: "Obtain 1 x Netherite Dragon Head Armor"
	task.6B10000000140003.title: "Obtain 1 x Netherite Dragon Neck Armor"
	task.6B10000000140004.title: "Obtain 1 x Netherite Dragon Body Armor"
	task.6B10000000140005.title: "Obtain 1 x Netherite Dragon Tail Armor"
	quest.5B10000000000014.title: "Draconic Industrial Partnership"
	quest.5B10000000000014.quest_desc: ["Raise a bonded dragon to Stage 3, ride it, and use its breath to operate the matching Dragonforge. This is the complete chain: Darknet expedition, specimen recovery, egg, husbandry, controlled breath, and reproducible Dragonsteel." "The dragon is a partner and weapons platform, not disposable forge equipment. If that ethical distinction seems needlessly sentimental, compare the size of its teeth with the size of your employment contract."]
	task.6B10000000150001.title: "Obtain 1 x Fire Dragonsteel Block"
	task.6B10000000150002.title: "Obtain 1 x Ice Dragonsteel Block"
	task.6B10000000150003.title: "Obtain 1 x Lightning Dragonsteel Block"
	quest.5B10000000000015.title: "Three Breaths, One Industrial Doctrine"
	quest.5B10000000000015.quest_desc: ["Compress the output of all three elemental Dragonforges into one block of Fire, Ice, and Lightning Dragonsteel. This is the auditable conclusion: every hunt, specimen chain, forge plant, and husbandry system is now independently productive." "You have converted three categories of mythological catastrophe into reproducible metallurgy. I would congratulate you more warmly, but that might encourage another category."]
	task.6B10000000160001.title: "Obtain 8 x Graphene-Coated Iron Ingot"
	task.6B10000000160002.title: "Obtain 4 x Fluix Crystal"
	task.6B10000000160003.title: "Obtain 2 x Logic Processor"
	quest.5B10000000000016.title: "Overworld Carrier Materials"
	quest.5B10000000000016.quest_desc: ["Prepare the carrier hardware before entering the Darknet: Graphene-Coated Iron, Fluix Crystals, and Logic Processors are all manufacturable with the civilization already operating in the Overworld." "Yes, preparation before entering the timed dragon dimension is permitted. I checked. It is even encouraged, despite the evidence supplied by your previous expeditions."]
	task.6B10000000170001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Temporal Core"
	quest.5B10000000000017.title: "Bounded Temporal Core"
	quest.5B10000000000017.quest_desc: ["Build a Darknet Temporal Core from a Virtual Machine Core, Quantum Cores, an Applied Energistics Energy Cell and Logic Processor, Graphene-Coated Iron, and Fiber Optics." "Every part is available through Overworld civilization and the Cyberspace fabrication chain. Requiring interplanetary metals to buy thirty more seconds would have been less engineering than hazing."]
	task.6B10000000180001.title: "Obtain 4 x Darknet Session Injector Tier I"
	quest.5B10000000000018.title: "Session Injector Tier I"
	quest.5B10000000000018.quest_desc: ["Build four Tier I Darknet Session Injectors. Each is consumed to add thirty seconds to an active session. Every higher tier consumes exactly one injector from the previous tier and doubles the granted time." "Thirty seconds sounds modest because you are comparing it with safety rather than with forced dimensional ejection during a dragon fight."]
	task.6B10000000190001.title: "Extend an active Darknet session"
	quest.5B10000000000019.title: "Field-Test the Carrier Extension"
	quest.5B10000000000019.quest_desc: ["Enter the Darknet and right-click any Session Injector while its carrier timer is active. The injector modifies and synchronizes Cyberspace's real countdown, consumes itself, and records this test automatically." "It does nothing outside the Darknet or without an active timer. I have attempted to engineer out every obvious way you might feed valuable hardware to empty air. Surprise me elsewhere."]
	task.6B100000001A0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Session Injector Tier II"
	quest.5B1000000000001A.title: "Session Injector Tier II"
	quest.5B1000000000001A.quest_desc: ["Add a pair of Logic Processors to the carrier package. Tier II adds sixty seconds: exactly twice Tier I."]
	task.6B100000001B0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Session Injector Tier III"
	quest.5B1000000000001B.title: "Session Injector Tier III"
	quest.5B1000000000001B.quest_desc: ["Install 1k Storage Components for a longer carrier-state buffer. Tier III adds one hundred twenty seconds, doubling Tier II."]
	task.6B100000001C0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Session Injector Tier IV"
	quest.5B1000000000001C.title: "Session Injector Tier IV"
	quest.5B1000000000001C.quest_desc: ["Introduce Calculation Processors to correct timing drift. Tier IV adds two hundred forty seconds, doubling Tier III."]
	task.6B100000001D0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Session Injector Tier V"
	quest.5B1000000000001D.title: "Session Injector Tier V"
	quest.5B1000000000001D.quest_desc: ["Expand the state buffer with 4k Storage Components. Tier V adds four hundred eighty seconds, doubling Tier IV."]
	task.6B100000001E0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Session Injector Tier VI"
	quest.5B1000000000001E.title: "Session Injector Tier VI"
	quest.5B1000000000001E.quest_desc: ["Replace the control package with Engineering Processors. Tier VI adds nine hundred sixty seconds, doubling Tier V."]
	task.6B100000001F0001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Session Injector Tier VII"
	quest.5B1000000000001F.title: "Session Injector Tier VII"
	quest.5B1000000000001F.quest_desc: ["Install 16k Storage Components. Tier VII adds one thousand nine hundred twenty seconds, doubling Tier VI, without requiring you to kill a dragon to obtain more time for killing dragons."]
	task.6B10000000200001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Session Injector Tier VIII"
	quest.5B10000000000020.title: "Session Injector Tier VIII"
	quest.5B10000000000020.quest_desc: ["Close the portable system with 64k Storage Components. Tier VIII adds three thousand eight hundred forty seconds: sixty-four minutes, exactly twice Tier VII and one hundred twenty-eight times Tier I." "If sixty-four additional minutes in the dragon-filled Darknet still feels insufficient, the device is no longer the limiting component in this operation."]
	task.6B10000000210001.title: "Obtain 1 x Darknet Anchor"
	quest.5B10000000000021.title: "Darknet Anchor"
	quest.5B10000000000021.quest_desc: ["Combine a Tier VIII Session Injector and Darknet Temporal Core with Quantum Cores, Virtual Machine Cores, a 128 cubed Spatial Storage Component, and a Dense Energy Cell. The result is an Applied Energistics Spatial Anchor retuned for a permanent Darknet carrier." "Place it only in the Darknet and connect it to a powered ME network. It binds to its placer, keeps its own network chunks loaded, and prevents the owner's active session timer from expiring anywhere in the dimension." "One anchor per operator. Breaking it, destroying it, or losing ME power terminates the tether and recalls you to the recorded Overworld position. Dying destroys it outright. Apparently immortality still requires maintenance."]
	// END GENERATED DARKNET DRACONIC CONVERGENCE
	// BEGIN GENERATED OLD WORLD NARRATIVE
	chapter_group.4F574E0000000001.title: "Old World Investigation"
	chapter.4F574E0000000002.title: "Old World Investigation"
	chapter.4F574E0000000002.subtitle: "Recover evidence where it was left; let the structures make the first argument."
	quest.4F57000000000001.title: "An Older Machine Language"
	quest.4F57000000000001.quest_desc: ["Build or recover a Create wrench before beginning the investigation. Familiar tools are the difference between archaeology and staring at a gearbox." "I have located an unusually intact roadside repair depot. Take the map. Do not dismantle the first machine you see merely because it has excellent brass fittings. — Charles"]
	task.4F57800000000001.title: "Obtain a Create Wrench"
	quest.4F57000000000002.title: "Roadside Automated Repair Depot"
	quest.4F57000000000002.quest_desc: ["Travel to the mapped Atlas Kinetic depot and enter the registered structure." "Read the building before opening its records: three service lanes, inspection trenches, controlled parts storage, and mechanical transfer equipment. This was ordinary roadside infrastructure, not a secret laboratory."]
	task.4F57800000000002.title: "Enter OWS-009"
	quest.4F57000000000003.title: "THEY WERE HERE FIRST"
	quest.4F57000000000003.quest_desc: ["Recover the stamped Atlas service plate and the transfer-maintenance manual from the depot records cage. The plate is consumed when submitted; the manual remains yours." "So. You are not inventing these principles from nothing. Atlas technicians standardized shafts, transfer lanes, service access, and lockout procedure long before the roads emptied. Recover their competence, not their complacency. — Charles"]
	task.4F57800000000003.title: "Return the Atlas Service Plate to Charles"
	task.4F57800000000004.title: "Recover the Atlas Maintenance Manual"
	quest.4F57000000000004.title: "The Hall Beyond the Garage"
	quest.4F57000000000004.quest_desc: ["Follow the Atlas map to a complete transfer hall. Its scale turns one roadside clue into an industrial system."]
	task.4F57800000000005.title: "Enter OWS-010"
	quest.4F57000000000005.title: "Ordinary Automation"
	quest.4F57000000000005.quest_desc: ["Recover the maintenance card. Atlas treated transfer tolerances and lockout schedules as ordinary infrastructure." "The resemblance is exact enough to be uncomfortable. They were here first, and they had already made it routine. — Charles"]
	task.4F57800000000006.title: "Return the Atlas Transfer Card"
	quest.4F57000000000010.title: "Food on Every Corner"
	quest.4F57000000000010.quest_desc: ["Bread is enough to begin asking how the old cities fed billions. Charles has marked a neighborhood VCF service depot."]
	task.4F57800000000010.title: "Produce a Staple Food"
	quest.4F57000000000011.title: "Neighborhood Culture Service"
	quest.4F57000000000011.quest_desc: ["Enter the VCF depot. Read its cooler banks, issue counter and return route before taking its records."]
	task.4F57800000000011.title: "Enter OWS-001"
	quest.4F57000000000012.title: "Food for a Billion — First Evidence"
	quest.4F57000000000012.quest_desc: ["The manifest proves Evercrop culture was mundane and everywhere. The exception log records the first failed seals and late returns."]
	task.4F57800000000012.title: "Return the VCF Service Manifest"
	task.4F57800000000013.title: "Recover the Return-Crate Log"
	quest.4F57000000000020.title: "Unexpected Maintenance"
	quest.4F57000000000020.quest_desc: ["A fluid pipe is enough context to understand the next record. Follow the PolyCore utility map."]
	task.4F57800000000020.title: "Understand Basic Fluid Handling"
	quest.4F57000000000021.title: "Utility Seal Failure Station"
	quest.4F57000000000021.quest_desc: ["Enter the ordinary pump station. The crisis is written in replacement stock, isolation paint and shorter intervals—not spectacle."]
	task.4F57800000000021.title: "Enter OWS-015"
	quest.4F57000000000022.title: "The Interval Collapses"
	quest.4F57000000000022.quest_desc: ["Twelve months. Six. Three. Weekly. Then blank. PolyCore knew the material was failing everywhere before anyone called it a catastrophe. — Charles"]
	task.4F57800000000022.title: "Return the PolyCore Failure Report"
	task.4F57800000000023.title: "Recover LOR-008"
	quest.4F57000000000013.title: "Emergency Community Grow Hall"
	quest.4F57000000000013.quest_desc: ["Enter the converted municipal hall. VCF racks and culture kits were deployed as public relief infrastructure during early containment."]
	task.4F57800000000014.title: "Enter OWS-002"
	quest.4F57000000000014.title: "Authorized Emergency Abundance"
	quest.4F57000000000014.quest_desc: ["Recover the signed grow authorization. This was policy, not an isolated experiment: governments used Evercrop when ordinary food logistics began to fail."]
	task.4F57800000000015.title: "Return the Emergency Grow Authorization"
	quest.4F57000000000015.title: "Cold-Chain Culture Nursery"
	quest.4F57000000000015.quest_desc: ["Follow the batch route into VCF cold storage. Dormant cultures moved from nursery vault to inspection to worldwide dispatch."]
	task.4F57800000000016.title: "Enter OWS-003"
	quest.4F57000000000016.title: "The Crop Was Already Everywhere"
	quest.4F57000000000016.quest_desc: ["The batch record connects dormancy to logistics. LOR-005 lists global license regions; there was no clean perimeter left to defend. Keep that conclusion provisional until more institutions corroborate it. — Charles"]
	task.4F57800000000017.title: "Return the VCF Culture Batch Record"
	task.4F57800000000018.title: "Recover LOR-005"
	quest.4F57000000000023.title: "Elastomer Exposure Array"
	quest.4F57000000000023.quest_desc: ["Enter the PolyCore laboratory and compare its four parallel chambers. The experiment was built to eliminate excuses."]
	task.4F57800000000024.title: "Enter OWS-016"
	quest.4F57000000000024.title: "Four Times Is a Result"
	quest.4F57000000000024.quest_desc: ["Recover the exposure authorization and Test 04. The same biological degradation repeated under controlled conditions. Unexpected maintenance had become a reproducible scientific fact."]
	task.4F57800000000025.title: "Return the Exposure Authorization"
	task.4F57800000000026.title: "Recover LOR-009"
	quest.4F57000000000030.title: "Mycological Vertical Farm Tower"
	quest.4F57000000000030.quest_desc: ["Enter the VCF tower and read it floor by floor: nutrient service below, cultivation above, then harvest, packaging and clean public-facing space."]
	task.4F57800000000030.title: "Enter OWS-004"
	quest.4F57000000000031.title: "FOOD FOR A BILLION"
	quest.4F57000000000031.quest_desc: ["Recover LOR-001, the Evercrop cultivation handbook. The tower was not a prototype; it was a repeatable industrial recipe for feeding a dense city."]
	task.4F57800000000031.title: "Return LOR-001 to Charles"
	quest.4F57000000000032.title: "PT-9 Symbiosis Pilot Laboratory"
	quest.4F57000000000032.quest_desc: ["Enter the pilot laboratory. Compare the culture chambers, bacterial-control rooms and polymer observation stations before disturbing the report."]
	task.4F57800000000032.title: "Enter OWS-006"
	quest.4F57000000000033.title: "THE PERFECT CROP"
	quest.4F57000000000033.quest_desc: ["Recover LOR-003. PT-9 documented beneficial bacteria protecting the crop while another observation showed polymer degradation. The same symbiosis that made Evercrop resilient may have made containment impossible. — Charles"]
	task.4F57800000000033.title: "Return LOR-003 to Charles"
	quest.4F57000000000040.title: "Bulk Crushing & Preparation Plant"
	quest.4F57000000000040.quest_desc: ["Enter the Atlas preparation plant. Crushers, mixers, feed lanes and dust handling turn the roadside transfer evidence into industrial-scale throughput."]
	task.4F57800000000040.title: "Enter OWS-012"
	quest.4F57000000000041.title: "The Cost of Throughput"
	quest.4F57000000000041.quest_desc: ["Recover the bulk-process manual. Atlas documented service failures as routine production constraints; scale came from maintaining the whole system, not merely making machines faster."]
	task.4F57800000000041.title: "Return the Atlas Bulk-Process Manual"
